I expect the same result from any order of iterations.

for example.

```JavaScript 
// span1
(
    // span2
    (
        // span3
        expr
    )
)
```

We will remove the parens and merge all comments. 
And we get the map

```
span_map {
    span2 -> span1,
    span3 -> span2,
}
```

Whether you get [`span1 span2`, `span3`] and then `span1 span2 span3` , or [`span1`, `span2 span3`] and then  `span1 span2 span3`, they should be same.

So FxHashMap should be fine.

But I don't know why AHashMap doesn't work, maybe it will lose data in some cases.

